{"lens":{"fp":"2997338152-24561","payload":"{\"score\":9,\"findings\":[{\"file\":\"plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh\",\"category\":\"startup cost\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"message\":\"plugin.sh runs a `$(cd ...)` subshell at load time to locate claim.sh, a fork the design decision document explicitly said to avoid by not having plugin.sh source claim.sh at all.\",\"quote\":\"_ccgl_plugin_dir=\\\"$(cd \\\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]%/*}\\\" 2>/dev/null || true; pwd)\\\"\",\"trigger\":\"Every time plugin.sh is loaded for the first time in a process (guarded by `_ZBUILD_CLAIM_GH_LABELS_LOADED`, so once per runner process). The design doc for this issue states: 'plugin.sh must not source core/claim/claim.sh — that would create a circular dependency and add a startup $(cd ...) subshell in plugin.sh's load path.' The code does exactly what the design said not to do.\",\"introduced\":true,\"fix\":\"code\"},{\"file\":\"core/claim/claim.sh\",\"category\":\"unnecessary subshell\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"message\":\"`_ccgl_read_holder` calls `$(_ccgl_backend)` — a subshell that only echoes a variable — while the other new functions in claim.sh (`_zbuild_claim_read_labels_into`, `_zbuild_claim_add_label_direct`) explicitly replaced the same pattern with `${ZBUILD_CLAIM_BACKEND:-gh}` to avoid the fork.\",\"quote\":\"case \\\"$(_ccgl_backend)\\\" in\",\"trigger\":\"When `zbuild:claimed` is already on the issue and `zbuild_claim_acquire` calls `_ccgl_read_holder` on the conflict path; not in a hot loop, but the inconsistency is introduced here while the design comments in the same file call it out as avoided elsewhere.\",\"introduced\":true,\"fix\":\"code\"}]}","files":{"/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh":"2e2649a7ef6be6c9ab172921cc93401399968c6a","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/claim/claim.sh":"9c5e4918b9c2dd16c79aecbdd522a427e77449b0"}},"scripts/lib/run-status-render.sh":{"fp":"226858007-26104:file:scripts/lib/run-status-render.sh","payload":"clean: no finding\n[]","files":{"/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/claim/claim.sh":"3ee1e638d8108c0b35dfdfb32c77febbc5ea4d0b","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh":"eaa14c26e667977fea02fc641fb31dc3ac5203d1","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/registry.sh":"3a46f76258dd2ab5d9b9288827f822cecffc56fc","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/discovery.sh":"127a064695f20869e15e14d04224342c02a489fb","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/scripts/lib/run-status-render.sh":"e66946ae97fcf967c5f77ee2ea2518de3b7fda3b"},"base":{"head":"a35e504edf2abbeecbb649a5e438ab9180e9f1ec","files":{}}},"core/claim/claim.sh":{"fp":"226858007-26104:file:core/claim/claim.sh","payload":"found: findings\n[{\"file\":\"core/claim/claim.sh\",\"category\":\"subshell overhead\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"message\":\"Two grep-based subshell spawns parse the `acquired` field from JSON on every acquire path, while `jq` is already imported and used immediately below for the `holder` field.\",\"quote\":\"_acquired_line=\\\"$(grep -o '\\\"acquired\\\":[[:space:]]*[a-z]*' <<< \\\"$json_out\\\" || true)\\\"\\n    acquired=\\\"$(grep -o 'true\\\\|false' <<< \\\"$_acquired_line\\\" || true)\\\"\",\"trigger\":\"Every successful `zbuild_claim_acquire` call on a run with an issue number: two subshell spawns run where one `jq` call would suffice.\",\"accepted_if\":\"The `acquired` boolean is extracted without spawning more subshell processes than the `holder` extraction already requires.\",\"introduced\":true,\"fix\":\"code\"}]","files":{"/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/claim/claim.sh":"3ee1e638d8108c0b35dfdfb32c77febbc5ea4d0b","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/wo